{"task_id": "Mbpp/903", "original_task_id": 903, "entry_point": "count_Unset_Bits", "prompt": "Write a python function to count the total unset bits from 1 to n.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef count_Unset_Bits(n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to count the total unset bits from 1 to n.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def count_Unset_Bits(n) :  \r\n    cnt = 0;  \r\n    for i in range(1,n + 1) : \r\n        temp = i;  \r\n        while (temp) :  \r\n            if (temp % 2 == 0) : \r\n                cnt += 1;  \r\n            temp = temp // 2;  \r\n    return cnt;  ", "tests": "assert count_Unset_Bits(2) == 1\nassert count_Unset_Bits(5) == 4\nassert count_Unset_Bits(14) == 17", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/933", "original_task_id": 933, "entry_point": "camel_to_snake", "prompt": "Write a function to convert camel case string to snake case string by using regex.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef camel_to_snake(text):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to convert camel case string to snake case string by using regex.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "import re\r\ndef camel_to_snake(text):\r\n  str1 = re.sub('(.)([A-Z][a-z]+)', r'\\1_\\2', text)\r\n  return re.sub('([a-z0-9])([A-Z])', r'\\1_\\2', str1).lower()", "tests": "assert camel_to_snake('GoogleAssistant') == 'google_assistant'\nassert camel_to_snake('ChromeCast') == 'chrome_cast'\nassert camel_to_snake('QuadCore') == 'quad_core'", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/806", "original_task_id": 806, "entry_point": "max_run_uppercase", "prompt": "Write a function to find maximum run of uppercase characters in the given string.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef max_run_uppercase(test_str):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find maximum run of uppercase characters in the given string.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def max_run_uppercase(test_str):\r\n  cnt = 0\r\n  res = 0\r\n  for idx in range(0, len(test_str)):\r\n    if test_str[idx].isupper():\r\n      cnt += 1\r\n    else:\r\n      res = cnt\r\n      cnt = 0\r\n  if test_str[len(test_str) - 1].isupper():\r\n    res = cnt\r\n  return (res)", "tests": "assert max_run_uppercase('GeMKSForGERksISBESt') == 5\nassert max_run_uppercase('PrECIOusMOVemENTSYT') == 6\nassert max_run_uppercase('GooGLEFluTTER') == 4", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/781", "original_task_id": 781, "entry_point": "count_Divisors", "prompt": "Write a python function to check whether the count of divisors is even or odd.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef count_Divisors(n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to check whether the count of divisors is even or odd.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "import math \r\ndef count_Divisors(n) : \r\n    count = 0\r\n    for i in range(1, (int)(math.sqrt(n)) + 2) : \r\n        if (n % i == 0) : \r\n            if( n // i == i) : \r\n                count = count + 1\r\n            else : \r\n                count = count + 2\r\n    if (count % 2 == 0) : \r\n        return (\"Even\") \r\n    else : \r\n        return (\"Odd\") ", "tests": "assert count_Divisors(10) == \"Even\"\nassert count_Divisors(100) == \"Odd\"\nassert count_Divisors(125) == \"Even\"", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
