{"task_id": "Mbpp/974", "original_task_id": 974, "entry_point": "min_sum_path", "prompt": "Write a function to find the minimum total path sum in the given triangle.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef min_sum_path(A):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find the minimum total path sum in the given triangle.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def min_sum_path(A): \r\n\tmemo = [None] * len(A) \r\n\tn = len(A) - 1\r\n\tfor i in range(len(A[n])): \r\n\t\tmemo[i] = A[n][i] \r\n\tfor i in range(len(A) - 2, -1,-1): \r\n\t\tfor j in range( len(A[i])): \r\n\t\t\tmemo[j] = A[i][j] + min(memo[j], \r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tmemo[j + 1]) \r\n\treturn memo[0]", "tests": "assert min_sum_path([[ 2 ], [3, 9 ], [1, 6, 7 ]]) == 6\nassert min_sum_path([[ 2 ], [3, 7 ], [8, 5, 6 ]]) == 10 \nassert min_sum_path([[ 3 ], [6, 4 ], [5, 2, 7 ]]) == 9", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/692", "original_task_id": 692, "entry_point": "last_Two_Digits", "prompt": "Write a python function to find the last two digits in factorial of a given number.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef last_Two_Digits(N):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to find the last two digits in factorial of a given number.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def last_Two_Digits(N): \r\n    if (N >= 10): \r\n        return\r\n    fac = 1\r\n    for i in range(1,N + 1): \r\n        fac = (fac * i) % 100\r\n    return (fac) ", "tests": "assert last_Two_Digits(7) == 40\nassert last_Two_Digits(5) == 20\nassert last_Two_Digits(2) == 2", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/938", "original_task_id": 938, "entry_point": "find_closet", "prompt": "Write a function to find three closest elements from three sorted arrays.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef find_closet(A, B, C, p, q, r):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find three closest elements from three sorted arrays.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "import sys \r\n\r\ndef find_closet(A, B, C, p, q, r): \r\n\tdiff = sys.maxsize \r\n\tres_i = 0\r\n\tres_j = 0\r\n\tres_k = 0\r\n\ti = 0\r\n\tj = 0\r\n\tk = 0\r\n\twhile(i < p and j < q and k < r): \r\n\t\tminimum = min(A[i], min(B[j], C[k])) \r\n\t\tmaximum = max(A[i], max(B[j], C[k])); \r\n\t\tif maximum-minimum < diff: \r\n\t\t\tres_i = i \r\n\t\t\tres_j = j \r\n\t\t\tres_k = k \r\n\t\t\tdiff = maximum - minimum; \r\n\t\tif diff == 0: \r\n\t\t\tbreak\r\n\t\tif A[i] == minimum: \r\n\t\t\ti = i+1\r\n\t\telif B[j] == minimum: \r\n\t\t\tj = j+1\r\n\t\telse: \r\n\t\t\tk = k+1\r\n\treturn A[res_i],B[res_j],C[res_k]", "tests": "assert find_closet([1, 4, 10],[2, 15, 20],[10, 12],3,3,2) == (10, 15, 10)\nassert find_closet([20, 24, 100],[2, 19, 22, 79, 800],[10, 12, 23, 24, 119],3,5,5) == (24, 22, 23)\nassert find_closet([2, 5, 11],[3, 16, 21],[11, 13],3,3,2) == (11, 16, 11)", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/871", "original_task_id": 871, "entry_point": "are_Rotations", "prompt": "Write a python function to check whether the given strings are rotations of each other or not.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef are_Rotations(string1, string2):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to check whether the given strings are rotations of each other or not.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def are_Rotations(string1,string2): \r\n    size1 = len(string1) \r\n    size2 = len(string2) \r\n    temp = '' \r\n    if size1 != size2: \r\n        return False\r\n    temp = string1 + string1 \r\n    if (temp.count(string2)> 0): \r\n        return True\r\n    else: \r\n        return False", "tests": "assert are_Rotations(\"abc\",\"cba\") == False\nassert are_Rotations(\"abcd\",\"cdba\") == False\nassert are_Rotations(\"abacd\",\"cdaba\") == True", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/862", "original_task_id": 862, "entry_point": "n_common_words", "prompt": "Write a function to find the occurrences of n most common words in a given text.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef n_common_words(text, n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find the occurrences of n most common words in a given text.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "from collections import Counter\r\nimport re\r\ndef n_common_words(text,n):\r\n  words = re.findall('\\w+',text)\r\n  n_common_words= Counter(words).most_common(n)\r\n  return list(n_common_words)", "tests": "assert n_common_words(\"python is a programming language\",1)==[('python', 1)]\nassert n_common_words(\"python is a programming language\",1)==[('python', 1)]\nassert n_common_words(\"python is a programming language\",5)==[('python', 1),('is', 1), ('a', 1), ('programming', 1), ('language', 1)]", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/650", "original_task_id": 650, "entry_point": "are_Equal", "prompt": "Write a python function to check whether the given two arrays are equal or not.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef are_Equal(arr1, arr2, n, m):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to check whether the given two arrays are equal or not.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def are_Equal(arr1,arr2,n,m):\r\n    if (n != m):\r\n        return False\r\n    arr1.sort()\r\n    arr2.sort()\r\n    for i in range(0,n - 1):\r\n        if (arr1[i] != arr2[i]):\r\n            return False\r\n    return True", "tests": "assert are_Equal([1,2,3],[3,2,1],3,3) == True\nassert are_Equal([1,1,1],[2,2,2],3,3) == False\nassert are_Equal([8,9],[4,5,6],2,3) == False", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/707", "original_task_id": 707, "entry_point": "count_Set_Bits", "prompt": "Write a python function to count the total set bits from 1 to n.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef count_Set_Bits(n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to count the total set bits from 1 to n.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def count_Set_Bits(n) :  \r\n    n += 1; \r\n    powerOf2 = 2;   \r\n    cnt = n // 2;  \r\n    while (powerOf2 <= n) : \r\n        totalPairs = n // powerOf2;  \r\n        cnt += (totalPairs // 2) * powerOf2;  \r\n        if (totalPairs & 1) : \r\n            cnt += (n % powerOf2) \r\n        else : \r\n            cnt += 0\r\n        powerOf2 <<= 1;    \r\n    return cnt;  ", "tests": "assert count_Set_Bits(16) == 33\nassert count_Set_Bits(2) == 2\nassert count_Set_Bits(14) == 28", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
