{"task_id": "Mbpp/664", "original_task_id": 664, "entry_point": "average_Even", "prompt": "Write a python function to find the average of even numbers till a given even number.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef average_Even(n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to find the average of even numbers till a given even number.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def average_Even(n) : \r\n    if (n% 2!= 0) : \r\n        return (\"Invalid Input\") \r\n        return -1  \r\n    sm = 0\r\n    count = 0\r\n    while (n>= 2) : \r\n        count = count+1\r\n        sm = sm+n \r\n        n = n-2\r\n    return sm // count ", "tests": "assert average_Even(2) == 2\nassert average_Even(4) == 3\nassert average_Even(100) == 51", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/785", "original_task_id": 785, "entry_point": "tuple_str_int", "prompt": "Write a function to convert tuple string to integer tuple.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef tuple_str_int(test_str):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to convert tuple string to integer tuple.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def tuple_str_int(test_str):\r\n  res = tuple(int(num) for num in test_str.replace('(', '').replace(')', '').replace('...', '').split(', '))\r\n  return (res) ", "tests": "assert tuple_str_int(\"(7, 8, 9)\") == (7, 8, 9)\nassert tuple_str_int(\"(1, 2, 3)\") == (1, 2, 3)\nassert tuple_str_int(\"(4, 5, 6)\") == (4, 5, 6)", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/966", "original_task_id": 966, "entry_point": "remove_empty", "prompt": "Write a function to remove an empty tuple from a list of tuples.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef remove_empty(tuple1):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to remove an empty tuple from a list of tuples.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def remove_empty(tuple1): #L = [(), (), ('',), ('a', 'b'), ('a', 'b', 'c'), ('d')]\r\n   tuple1 = [t for t in tuple1 if t]\r\n   return tuple1", "tests": "assert remove_empty([(), (), ('',), ('a', 'b'), ('a', 'b', 'c'), ('d')])==[('',), ('a', 'b'), ('a', 'b', 'c'), 'd']  \nassert remove_empty([(), (), ('',), (\"python\"), (\"program\")])==[('',), (\"python\"), (\"program\")]  \nassert remove_empty([(), (), ('',), (\"java\")])==[('',),(\"java\") ]  ", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/842", "original_task_id": 842, "entry_point": "get_odd_occurence", "prompt": "Write a function to find the number which occurs for odd number of times in the given array.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef get_odd_occurence(arr, arr_size):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find the number which occurs for odd number of times in the given array.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def get_odd_occurence(arr, arr_size):\r\n  for i in range(0, arr_size):\r\n    count = 0\r\n    for j in range(0, arr_size):\r\n      if arr[i] == arr[j]:\r\n        count += 1\r\n    if (count % 2 != 0):\r\n      return arr[i]\r\n  return -1", "tests": "assert get_odd_occurence([2, 3, 5, 4, 5, 2, 4, 3, 5, 2, 4, 4, 2], 13) == 5\nassert get_odd_occurence([1, 2, 3, 2, 3, 1, 3], 7) == 3\nassert get_odd_occurence([5, 7, 2, 7, 5, 2, 5], 7) == 5", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/778", "original_task_id": 778, "entry_point": "pack_consecutive_duplicates", "prompt": "Write a function to pack consecutive duplicates of a given list elements into sublists.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef pack_consecutive_duplicates(list1):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to pack consecutive duplicates of a given list elements into sublists.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "from itertools import groupby\r\ndef pack_consecutive_duplicates(list1):\r\n    return [list(group) for key, group in groupby(list1)]", "tests": "assert pack_consecutive_duplicates([0, 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 4, 5, 6, 6, 6, 7, 8, 9, 4, 4])==[[0, 0], [1], [2], [3], [4, 4], [5], [6, 6, 6], [7], [8], [9], [4, 4]]\nassert pack_consecutive_duplicates([10, 10, 15, 19, 18, 18, 17, 26, 26, 17, 18, 10])==[[10, 10], [15], [19], [18, 18], [17], [26, 26], [17], [18], [10]]\nassert pack_consecutive_duplicates(['a', 'a', 'b', 'c', 'd', 'd'])==[['a', 'a'], ['b'], ['c'], ['d', 'd']]", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/791", "original_task_id": 791, "entry_point": "remove_nested", "prompt": "Write a function to remove the nested record from the given tuple.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef remove_nested(test_tup):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to remove the nested record from the given tuple.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def remove_nested(test_tup):\r\n  res = tuple()\r\n  for count, ele in enumerate(test_tup):\r\n    if not isinstance(ele, tuple):\r\n      res = res + (ele, )\r\n  return (res) ", "tests": "assert remove_nested((1, 5, 7, (4, 6), 10)) == (1, 5, 7, 10)\nassert remove_nested((2, 6, 8, (5, 7), 11)) == (2, 6, 8, 11)\nassert remove_nested((3, 7, 9, (6, 8), 12)) == (3, 7, 9, 12)", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/874", "original_task_id": 874, "entry_point": "check_Concat", "prompt": "Write a python function to check if the string is a concatenation of another string.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef check_Concat(str1, str2):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to check if the string is a concatenation of another string.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def check_Concat(str1,str2):\r\n    N = len(str1)\r\n    M = len(str2)\r\n    if (N % M != 0):\r\n        return False\r\n    for i in range(N):\r\n        if (str1[i] != str2[i % M]):\r\n            return False         \r\n    return True", "tests": "assert check_Concat(\"abcabcabc\",\"abc\") == True\nassert check_Concat(\"abcab\",\"abc\") == False\nassert check_Concat(\"aba\",\"ab\") == False", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/662", "original_task_id": 662, "entry_point": "sorted_dict", "prompt": "Write a function to sort a list in a dictionary.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef sorted_dict(dict1):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to sort a list in a dictionary.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def sorted_dict(dict1):\r\n  sorted_dict = {x: sorted(y) for x, y in dict1.items()}\r\n  return sorted_dict", "tests": "assert sorted_dict({'n1': [2, 3, 1], 'n2': [5, 1, 2], 'n3': [3, 2, 4]})=={'n1': [1, 2, 3], 'n2': [1, 2, 5], 'n3': [2, 3, 4]}\nassert sorted_dict({'n1': [25,37,41], 'n2': [41,54,63], 'n3': [29,38,93]})=={'n1': [25, 37, 41], 'n2': [41, 54, 63], 'n3': [29, 38, 93]}\nassert sorted_dict({'n1': [58,44,56], 'n2': [91,34,58], 'n3': [100,200,300]})=={'n1': [44, 56, 58], 'n2': [34, 58, 91], 'n3': [100, 200, 300]}", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/734", "original_task_id": 734, "entry_point": "sum_Of_Subarray_Prod", "prompt": "Write a python function to find sum of products of all possible subarrays.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef sum_Of_Subarray_Prod(arr, n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to find sum of products of all possible subarrays.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def sum_Of_Subarray_Prod(arr,n):\r\n    ans = 0\r\n    res = 0\r\n    i = n - 1\r\n    while (i >= 0):\r\n        incr = arr[i]*(1 + res)\r\n        ans += incr\r\n        res = incr\r\n        i -= 1\r\n    return (ans)", "tests": "assert sum_Of_Subarray_Prod([1,2,3],3) == 20\nassert sum_Of_Subarray_Prod([1,2],2) == 5\nassert sum_Of_Subarray_Prod([1,2,3,4],4) == 84", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/926", "original_task_id": 926, "entry_point": "rencontres_number", "prompt": "Write a function to find n-th rencontres number.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef rencontres_number(n, m):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find n-th rencontres number.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def binomial_coeffi(n, k): \r\n\tif (k == 0 or k == n): \r\n\t\treturn 1\r\n\treturn (binomial_coeffi(n - 1, k - 1) \r\n\t\t+ binomial_coeffi(n - 1, k)) \r\ndef rencontres_number(n, m): \r\n\tif (n == 0 and m == 0): \r\n\t\treturn 1\r\n\tif (n == 1 and m == 0): \r\n\t\treturn 0\r\n\tif (m == 0): \r\n\t\treturn ((n - 1) * (rencontres_number(n - 1, 0)+ rencontres_number(n - 2, 0))) \r\n\treturn (binomial_coeffi(n, m) * rencontres_number(n - m, 0))", "tests": "assert rencontres_number(7, 2) == 924\nassert rencontres_number(3, 0) == 2\nassert rencontres_number(3, 1) == 3", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/686", "original_task_id": 686, "entry_point": "freq_element", "prompt": "Write a function to find the frequency of each element in the given list.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef freq_element(test_tup):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find the frequency of each element in the given list.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "from collections import defaultdict \r\ndef freq_element(test_tup):\r\n  res = defaultdict(int)\r\n  for ele in test_tup:\r\n    res[ele] += 1\r\n  return (str(dict(res))) ", "tests": "assert freq_element((4, 5, 4, 5, 6, 6, 5, 5, 4) ) == '{4: 3, 5: 4, 6: 2}'\nassert freq_element((7, 8, 8, 9, 4, 7, 6, 5, 4) ) == '{7: 2, 8: 2, 9: 1, 4: 2, 6: 1, 5: 1}'\nassert freq_element((1, 4, 3, 1, 4, 5, 2, 6, 2, 7) ) == '{1: 2, 4: 2, 3: 1, 5: 1, 2: 2, 6: 1, 7: 1}'", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
