{"task_id": "Mbpp/904", "original_task_id": 904, "entry_point": "even_num", "prompt": "Write a function to return true if the given number is even else return false.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef even_num(x):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to return true if the given number is even else return false.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def even_num(x):\r\n  if x%2==0:\r\n     return True\r\n  else:\r\n    return False", "tests": "assert even_num(13.5)==False\nassert even_num(0)==True\nassert even_num(-9)==False", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/760", "original_task_id": 760, "entry_point": "unique_Element", "prompt": "Write a python function to check whether an array contains only one distinct element or not.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef unique_Element(arr, n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to check whether an array contains only one distinct element or not.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def unique_Element(arr,n):\r\n    s = set(arr)\r\n    if (len(s) == 1):\r\n        return ('YES')\r\n    else:\r\n        return ('NO')", "tests": "assert unique_Element([1,1,1],3) == 'YES'\nassert unique_Element([1,2,1,2],4) == 'NO'\nassert unique_Element([1,2,3,4,5],5) == 'NO'", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/960", "original_task_id": 960, "entry_point": "get_noOfways", "prompt": "Write a function to solve tiling problem.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef get_noOfways(n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to solve tiling problem.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def get_noOfways(n):\r\n    if (n == 0):\r\n        return 0;\r\n    if (n == 1):\r\n        return 1; \r\n    return get_noOfways(n - 1) + get_noOfways(n - 2);", "tests": "assert get_noOfways(4)==3\nassert get_noOfways(3)==2\nassert get_noOfways(5)==5", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/620", "original_task_id": 620, "entry_point": "largest_subset", "prompt": "Write a function to find the largest subset where each pair is divisible.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef largest_subset(a, n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find the largest subset where each pair is divisible.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def largest_subset(a, n):\r\n\tdp = [0 for i in range(n)]\r\n\tdp[n - 1] = 1; \r\n\tfor i in range(n - 2, -1, -1):\r\n\t\tmxm = 0;\r\n\t\tfor j in range(i + 1, n):\r\n\t\t\tif a[j] % a[i] == 0 or a[i] % a[j] == 0:\r\n\t\t\t\tmxm = max(mxm, dp[j])\r\n\t\tdp[i] = 1 + mxm\r\n\treturn max(dp)", "tests": "assert largest_subset([ 1, 3, 6, 13, 17, 18 ], 6) == 4\nassert largest_subset([10, 5, 3, 15, 20], 5) == 3\nassert largest_subset([18, 1, 3, 6, 13, 17], 6) == 4", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/603", "original_task_id": 603, "entry_point": "get_ludic", "prompt": "Write a function to get a lucid number smaller than or equal to n.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef get_ludic(n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to get a lucid number smaller than or equal to n.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def get_ludic(n):\r\n\tludics = []\r\n\tfor i in range(1, n + 1):\r\n\t\tludics.append(i)\r\n\tindex = 1\r\n\twhile(index != len(ludics)):\r\n\t\tfirst_ludic = ludics[index]\r\n\t\tremove_index = index + first_ludic\r\n\t\twhile(remove_index < len(ludics)):\r\n\t\t\tludics.remove(ludics[remove_index])\r\n\t\t\tremove_index = remove_index + first_ludic - 1\r\n\t\tindex += 1\r\n\treturn ludics", "tests": "assert get_ludic(10) == [1, 2, 3, 5, 7]\nassert get_ludic(25) == [1, 2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17, 23, 25]\nassert get_ludic(45) == [1, 2, 3, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17, 23, 25, 29, 37, 41, 43]", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/956", "original_task_id": 956, "entry_point": "split_list", "prompt": "Write a function to split the given string at uppercase letters by using regex.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef split_list(text):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to split the given string at uppercase letters by using regex.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "import re\r\ndef split_list(text):\r\n  return (re.findall('[A-Z][^A-Z]*', text))", "tests": "assert split_list(\"LearnToBuildAnythingWithGoogle\") == ['Learn', 'To', 'Build', 'Anything', 'With', 'Google']\nassert split_list(\"ApmlifyingTheBlack+DeveloperCommunity\") == ['Apmlifying', 'The', 'Black+', 'Developer', 'Community']\nassert split_list(\"UpdateInTheGoEcoSystem\") == ['Update', 'In', 'The', 'Go', 'Eco', 'System']", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
