{"task_id": "Mbpp/660", "original_task_id": 660, "entry_point": "find_Points", "prompt": "Write a python function to choose points from two ranges such that no point lies in both the ranges.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef find_Points(l1, r1, l2, r2):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to choose points from two ranges such that no point lies in both the ranges.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def find_Points(l1,r1,l2,r2): \r\n    x = min(l1,l2) if (l1 != l2) else -1\r\n    y = max(r1,r2) if (r1 != r2) else -1\r\n    return (x,y)", "tests": "assert find_Points(5,10,1,5) == (1,10)\nassert find_Points(3,5,7,9) == (3,9)\nassert find_Points(1,5,2,8) == (1,8)", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/849", "original_task_id": 849, "entry_point": "Sum", "prompt": "Write a python function to find sum of all prime divisors of a given number.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef Sum(N):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to find sum of all prime divisors of a given number.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def Sum(N): \r\n    SumOfPrimeDivisors = [0]*(N + 1)   \r\n    for i in range(2,N + 1) : \r\n        if (SumOfPrimeDivisors[i] == 0) : \r\n            for j in range(i,N + 1,i) : \r\n                SumOfPrimeDivisors[j] += i           \r\n    return SumOfPrimeDivisors[N] ", "tests": "assert Sum(60) == 10\nassert Sum(39) == 16\nassert Sum(40) == 7", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/921", "original_task_id": 921, "entry_point": "chunk_tuples", "prompt": "Write a function to perform chunking of tuples each of size n.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef chunk_tuples(test_tup, N):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to perform chunking of tuples each of size n.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def chunk_tuples(test_tup, N):\r\n  res = [test_tup[i : i + N] for i in range(0, len(test_tup), N)]\r\n  return (res) ", "tests": "assert chunk_tuples((10, 4, 5, 6, 7, 6, 8, 3, 4), 3) == [(10, 4, 5), (6, 7, 6), (8, 3, 4)]\nassert chunk_tuples((1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9), 2) == [(1, 2), (3, 4), (5, 6), (7, 8), (9,)]\nassert chunk_tuples((11, 14, 16, 17, 19, 21, 22, 25), 4) == [(11, 14, 16, 17), (19, 21, 22, 25)]", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/607", "original_task_id": 607, "entry_point": "find_literals", "prompt": "Write a function to search a literals string in a string and also find the location within the original string where the pattern occurs by using regex.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef find_literals(text, pattern):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to search a literals string in a string and also find the location within the original string where the pattern occurs by using regex.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "import re\r\npattern = 'fox'\r\ntext = 'The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.'\r\ndef find_literals(text, pattern):\r\n  match = re.search(pattern, text)\r\n  s = match.start()\r\n  e = match.end()\r\n  return (match.re.pattern, s, e)", "tests": "assert find_literals('The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.', 'fox') == ('fox', 16, 19)\nassert find_literals('Its been a very crazy procedure right', 'crazy') == ('crazy', 16, 21)\nassert find_literals('Hardest choices required strongest will', 'will') == ('will', 35, 39)", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
