{"task_id": "Mbpp/971", "original_task_id": 971, "entry_point": "maximum_segments", "prompt": "Write a function to find the maximum number of segments of lengths a, b and c that can be formed from n.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef maximum_segments(n, a, b, c):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find the maximum number of segments of lengths a, b and c that can be formed from n.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def maximum_segments(n, a, b, c) : \r\n\tdp = [-1] * (n + 10) \r\n\tdp[0] = 0\r\n\tfor i in range(0, n) : \r\n\t\tif (dp[i] != -1) : \r\n\t\t\tif(i + a <= n ): \r\n\t\t\t\tdp[i + a] = max(dp[i] + 1, \r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdp[i + a]) \r\n\t\t\tif(i + b <= n ): \r\n\t\t\t\tdp[i + b] = max(dp[i] + 1, \r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdp[i + b]) \r\n\t\t\tif(i + c <= n ): \r\n\t\t\t\tdp[i + c] = max(dp[i] + 1, \r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tdp[i + c]) \r\n\treturn dp[n]", "tests": "assert maximum_segments(7, 5, 2, 5) == 2\nassert maximum_segments(17, 2, 1, 3) == 17\nassert maximum_segments(18, 16, 3, 6) == 6", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/724", "original_task_id": 724, "entry_point": "power_base_sum", "prompt": "Write a function to calculate the sum of all digits of the base to the specified power.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef power_base_sum(base, power):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to calculate the sum of all digits of the base to the specified power.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def power_base_sum(base, power):\r\n    return sum([int(i) for i in str(pow(base, power))])", "tests": "assert power_base_sum(2,100)==115\nassert power_base_sum(8,10)==37\nassert power_base_sum(8,15)==62", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/771", "original_task_id": 771, "entry_point": "check_expression", "prompt": "Write a function to check if the given expression is balanced or not.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef check_expression(exp):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to check if the given expression is balanced or not.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "from collections import deque\r\ndef check_expression(exp):\r\n    if len(exp) & 1:\r\n        return False\r\n    stack = deque()\r\n    for ch in exp:\r\n        if ch == '(' or ch == '{' or ch == '[':\r\n            stack.append(ch)\r\n        if ch == ')' or ch == '}' or ch == ']':\r\n            if not stack:\r\n                return False\r\n            top = stack.pop()\r\n            if (top == '(' and ch != ')') or (top == '{' and ch != '}' or (top == '[' and ch != ']')):\r\n                return False\r\n    return not stack", "tests": "assert check_expression(\"{()}[{}]\") == True\nassert check_expression(\"{()}[{]\") == False\nassert check_expression(\"{()}[{}][]({})\") == True", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/868", "original_task_id": 868, "entry_point": "length_Of_Last_Word", "prompt": "Write a python function to find the length of the last word in a given string.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef length_Of_Last_Word(a):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to find the length of the last word in a given string.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def length_Of_Last_Word(a): \r\n    l = 0\r\n    x = a.strip() \r\n    for i in range(len(x)): \r\n        if x[i] == \" \": \r\n            l = 0\r\n        else: \r\n            l += 1\r\n    return l ", "tests": "assert length_Of_Last_Word(\"python language\") == 8\nassert length_Of_Last_Word(\"PHP\") == 3\nassert length_Of_Last_Word(\"\") == 0", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/634", "original_task_id": 634, "entry_point": "even_Power_Sum", "prompt": "Write a python function to find the sum of fourth power of first n even natural numbers.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef even_Power_Sum(n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to find the sum of fourth power of first n even natural numbers.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def even_Power_Sum(n): \r\n    sum = 0; \r\n    for i in range(1,n + 1): \r\n        j = 2*i; \r\n        sum = sum + (j*j*j*j); \r\n    return sum; ", "tests": "assert even_Power_Sum(2) == 272\nassert even_Power_Sum(3) == 1568\nassert even_Power_Sum(4) == 5664", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/901", "original_task_id": 901, "entry_point": "smallest_multiple", "prompt": "Write a function to find the smallest multiple of the first n numbers.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef smallest_multiple(n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find the smallest multiple of the first n numbers.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def smallest_multiple(n):\r\n    if (n<=2):\r\n      return n\r\n    i = n * 2\r\n    factors = [number  for number in range(n, 1, -1) if number * 2 > n]\r\n    while True:\r\n        for a in factors:\r\n            if i % a != 0:\r\n                i += n\r\n                break\r\n            if (a == factors[-1] and i % a == 0):\r\n                return i", "tests": "assert smallest_multiple(13)==360360\nassert smallest_multiple(2)==2\nassert smallest_multiple(1)==1", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/619", "original_task_id": 619, "entry_point": "move_num", "prompt": "Write a function to move all the numbers in it to the given string.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef move_num(test_str):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to move all the numbers in it to the given string.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def move_num(test_str):\r\n  res = ''\r\n  dig = ''\r\n  for ele in test_str:\r\n    if ele.isdigit():\r\n      dig += ele\r\n    else:\r\n      res += ele\r\n  res += dig\r\n  return (res) ", "tests": "assert move_num('I1love143you55three3000thousand') == 'Iloveyouthreethousand1143553000'\nassert move_num('Avengers124Assemble') == 'AvengersAssemble124'\nassert move_num('Its11our12path13to14see15things16do17things') == 'Itsourpathtoseethingsdothings11121314151617'", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/727", "original_task_id": 727, "entry_point": "remove_char", "prompt": "Write a function to remove all characters except letters and numbers using regex\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef remove_char(S):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to remove all characters except letters and numbers using regex", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "import re \r\ndef remove_char(S):\r\n  result = re.sub('[\\W_]+', '', S) \r\n  return result", "tests": "assert remove_char(\"123abcjw:, .@! eiw\") == '123abcjweiw'\nassert remove_char(\"Hello1234:, ! Howare33u\") == 'Hello1234Howare33u'\nassert remove_char(\"Cool543Triks@:, Make@987Trips\") == 'Cool543TriksMake987Trips' ", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
