{"task_id": "Mbpp/622", "original_task_id": 622, "entry_point": "get_median", "prompt": "Write a function to find the median of two sorted arrays of same size.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef get_median(arr1, arr2, n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find the median of two sorted arrays of same size.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def get_median(arr1, arr2, n):\r\n  i = 0\r\n  j = 0\r\n  m1 = -1\r\n  m2 = -1\r\n  count = 0\r\n  while count < n + 1:\r\n    count += 1\r\n    if i == n:\r\n      m1 = m2\r\n      m2 = arr2[0]\r\n      break\r\n    elif j == n:\r\n      m1 = m2\r\n      m2 = arr1[0]\r\n      break\r\n    if arr1[i] <= arr2[j]:\r\n      m1 = m2\r\n      m2 = arr1[i]\r\n      i += 1\r\n    else:\r\n      m1 = m2\r\n      m2 = arr2[j]\r\n      j += 1\r\n  return (m1 + m2)/2", "tests": "assert get_median([1, 12, 15, 26, 38], [2, 13, 17, 30, 45], 5) == 16.0\nassert get_median([2, 4, 8, 9], [7, 13, 19, 28], 4) == 8.5\nassert get_median([3, 6, 14, 23, 36, 42], [2, 18, 27, 39, 49, 55], 6) == 25.0", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
