{"task_id": "Mbpp/601", "original_task_id": 601, "entry_point": "max_chain_length", "prompt": "Write a function to find the longest chain which can be formed from the given set of pairs.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef max_chain_length(arr, n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find the longest chain which can be formed from the given set of pairs.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "class Pair(object): \r\n\tdef __init__(self, a, b): \r\n\t\tself.a = a \r\n\t\tself.b = b \r\ndef max_chain_length(arr, n): \r\n\tmax = 0\r\n\tmcl = [1 for i in range(n)] \r\n\tfor i in range(1, n): \r\n\t\tfor j in range(0, i): \r\n\t\t\tif (arr[i].a > arr[j].b and\r\n\t\t\t\tmcl[i] < mcl[j] + 1): \r\n\t\t\t\tmcl[i] = mcl[j] + 1\r\n\tfor i in range(n): \r\n\t\tif (max < mcl[i]): \r\n\t\t\tmax = mcl[i] \r\n\treturn max", "tests": "assert max_chain_length([Pair(5, 24), Pair(15, 25),Pair(27, 40), Pair(50, 60)], 4) == 3\nassert max_chain_length([Pair(1, 2), Pair(3, 4),Pair(5, 6), Pair(7, 8)], 4) == 4\nassert max_chain_length([Pair(19, 10), Pair(11, 12),Pair(13, 14), Pair(15, 16), Pair(31, 54)], 5) == 5", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/914", "original_task_id": 914, "entry_point": "is_Two_Alter", "prompt": "Write a python function to check whether the given string is made up of two alternating characters or not.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef is_Two_Alter(s):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to check whether the given string is made up of two alternating characters or not.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def is_Two_Alter(s):  \r\n    for i in range (len( s) - 2) : \r\n        if (s[i] != s[i + 2]) : \r\n            return False\r\n    if (s[0] == s[1]): \r\n        return False\r\n    return True", "tests": "assert is_Two_Alter(\"abab\") == True\nassert is_Two_Alter(\"aaaa\") == False\nassert is_Two_Alter(\"xyz\") == False", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/955", "original_task_id": 955, "entry_point": "is_abundant", "prompt": "Write a function to find out, if the given number is abundant.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef is_abundant(n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find out, if the given number is abundant.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def is_abundant(n):\r\n    fctrsum = sum([fctr for fctr in range(1, n) if n % fctr == 0])\r\n    return fctrsum > n", "tests": "assert is_abundant(12)==True\nassert is_abundant(13)==False\nassert is_abundant(9)==False", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/958", "original_task_id": 958, "entry_point": "int_to_roman", "prompt": "Write a function to convert an integer into a roman numeral.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef int_to_roman(num):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to convert an integer into a roman numeral.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def int_to_roman( num):\r\n        val = [1000, 900, 500, 400,100, 90, 50, 40,10, 9, 5, 4,1]\r\n        syb = [\"M\", \"CM\", \"D\", \"CD\",\"C\", \"XC\", \"L\", \"XL\",\"X\", \"IX\", \"V\", \"IV\",\"I\"]\r\n        roman_num = ''\r\n        i = 0\r\n        while  num > 0:\r\n            for _ in range(num // val[i]):\r\n                roman_num += syb[i]\r\n                num -= val[i]\r\n            i += 1\r\n        return roman_num", "tests": "assert int_to_roman(1)==(\"I\")\nassert int_to_roman(50)==(\"L\")\nassert int_to_roman(4)==(\"IV\")", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
