{"task_id": "Mbpp/795", "original_task_id": 795, "entry_point": "cheap_items", "prompt": "Write a function to find the n - cheap price items from a given dataset using heap queue algorithm.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef cheap_items(items, n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find the n - cheap price items from a given dataset using heap queue algorithm.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "import heapq\r\ndef cheap_items(items,n):\r\n  cheap_items = heapq.nsmallest(n, items, key=lambda s: s['price'])\r\n  return cheap_items", "tests": "assert cheap_items([{'name': 'Item-1', 'price': 101.1},{'name': 'Item-2', 'price': 555.22}],1)==[{'name': 'Item-1', 'price': 101.1}]\nassert cheap_items([{'name': 'Item-1', 'price': 101.1},{'name': 'Item-2', 'price': 555.22}],2)==[{'name': 'Item-1', 'price': 101.1},{'name': 'Item-2', 'price': 555.22}]\nassert cheap_items([{'name': 'Item-1', 'price': 101.1},{'name': 'Item-2', 'price': 555.22}, {'name': 'Item-3', 'price': 45.09},{'name': 'Item-4', 'price': 22.75}],1)==[{'name': 'Item-4', 'price': 22.75}]", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/884", "original_task_id": 884, "entry_point": "all_Bits_Set_In_The_Given_Range", "prompt": "Write a python function to check whether all the bits are within a given range or not.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef all_Bits_Set_In_The_Given_Range(n, l, r):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to check whether all the bits are within a given range or not.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def all_Bits_Set_In_The_Given_Range(n,l,r): \r\n    num = ((1 << r) - 1) ^ ((1 << (l - 1)) - 1) \r\n    new_num = n & num \r\n    if (num == new_num): \r\n        return True\r\n    return False", "tests": "assert all_Bits_Set_In_The_Given_Range(10,2,1) == True \nassert all_Bits_Set_In_The_Given_Range(5,2,4) == False\nassert all_Bits_Set_In_The_Given_Range(22,2,3) == True ", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/829", "original_task_id": 829, "entry_point": "second_frequent", "prompt": "Write a function to find out the second most repeated (or frequent) string in the given sequence.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef second_frequent(input):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find out the second most repeated (or frequent) string in the given sequence.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "from collections import Counter \r\n\t\r\ndef second_frequent(input): \r\n\tdict = Counter(input) \r\n\tvalue = sorted(dict.values(), reverse=True)  \r\n\tsecond_large = value[1] \r\n\tfor (key, val) in dict.items(): \r\n\t\tif val == second_large: \r\n\t\t\treturn (key) ", "tests": "assert second_frequent(['aaa','bbb','ccc','bbb','aaa','aaa']) == 'bbb'\nassert second_frequent(['abc','bcd','abc','bcd','bcd','bcd']) == 'abc'\nassert second_frequent(['cdma','gsm','hspa','gsm','cdma','cdma']) == 'gsm'", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/845", "original_task_id": 845, "entry_point": "find_Digits", "prompt": "Write a python function to count the number of digits in factorial of a given number.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef find_Digits(n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to count the number of digits in factorial of a given number.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "import math \r\ndef find_Digits(n): \r\n    if (n < 0): \r\n        return 0;\r\n    if (n <= 1): \r\n        return 1; \r\n    x = ((n * math.log10(n / math.e) + math.log10(2 * math.pi * n) /2.0)); \r\n    return math.floor(x) + 1; ", "tests": "assert find_Digits(7) == 4\nassert find_Digits(5) == 3\nassert find_Digits(4) == 2", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/631", "original_task_id": 631, "entry_point": "replace_spaces", "prompt": "Write a function to replace whitespaces with an underscore and vice versa in a given string by using regex.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef replace_spaces(text):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to replace whitespaces with an underscore and vice versa in a given string by using regex.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "import re\r\ntext = 'Python Exercises'\r\ndef replace_spaces(text):\r\n  text =text.replace (\" \", \"_\")\r\n  return (text)\r\n  text =text.replace (\"_\", \" \")\r\n  return (text)", "tests": "assert replace_spaces('Jumanji The Jungle') == 'Jumanji_The_Jungle'\nassert replace_spaces('The Avengers') == 'The_Avengers'\nassert replace_spaces('Fast and Furious') == 'Fast_and_Furious'", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/787", "original_task_id": 787, "entry_point": "text_match_three", "prompt": "Write a function that matches a string that has an a followed by three 'b'.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef text_match_three(text):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function that matches a string that has an a followed by three 'b'.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "import re\r\ndef text_match_three(text):\r\n        patterns = 'ab{3}?'\r\n        if re.search(patterns,  text):\r\n                return 'Found a match!'\r\n        else:\r\n                return('Not matched!')", "tests": "assert text_match_three(\"ac\")==('Not matched!')\nassert text_match_three(\"dc\")==('Not matched!')\nassert text_match_three(\"abbbba\")==('Found a match!')", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
