{"task_id": "Mbpp/911", "original_task_id": 911, "entry_point": "maximum_product", "prompt": "Write a function to compute maximum product of three numbers of a given array of integers using heap queue algorithm.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef maximum_product(nums):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to compute maximum product of three numbers of a given array of integers using heap queue algorithm.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def maximum_product(nums):\r\n    import heapq\r\n    a, b = heapq.nlargest(3, nums), heapq.nsmallest(2, nums)\r\n    return max(a[0] * a[1] * a[2], a[0] * b[0] * b[1])", "tests": "assert maximum_product( [12, 74, 9, 50, 61, 41])==225700\nassert maximum_product([25, 35, 22, 85, 14, 65, 75, 25, 58])==414375\nassert maximum_product([18, 14, 10, 9, 8, 7, 9, 3, 2, 4, 1])==2520", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
