{"task_id": "Mbpp/909", "original_task_id": 909, "entry_point": "previous_palindrome", "prompt": "Write a function to find the previous palindrome of a specified number.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef previous_palindrome(num):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find the previous palindrome of a specified number.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def previous_palindrome(num):\r\n    for x in range(num-1,0,-1):\r\n        if str(x) == str(x)[::-1]:\r\n            return x", "tests": "assert previous_palindrome(99)==88\nassert previous_palindrome(1221)==1111\nassert previous_palindrome(120)==111", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/839", "original_task_id": 839, "entry_point": "sort_tuple", "prompt": "Write a function to sort the tuples alphabetically by the first item of each tuple.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef sort_tuple(tup):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to sort the tuples alphabetically by the first item of each tuple.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def sort_tuple(tup): \r\n\tn = len(tup) \r\n\tfor i in range(n): \r\n\t\tfor j in range(n-i-1): \r\n\t\t\tif tup[j][0] > tup[j + 1][0]: \r\n\t\t\t\ttup[j], tup[j + 1] = tup[j + 1], tup[j] \r\n\treturn tup", "tests": "assert sort_tuple([(\"Amana\", 28), (\"Zenat\", 30), (\"Abhishek\", 29),(\"Nikhil\", 21), (\"B\", \"C\")]) == [('Abhishek', 29), ('Amana', 28), ('B', 'C'), ('Nikhil', 21), ('Zenat', 30)]\nassert sort_tuple([(\"aaaa\", 28), (\"aa\", 30), (\"bab\", 29), (\"bb\", 21), (\"csa\", \"C\")]) == [('aa', 30), ('aaaa', 28), ('bab', 29), ('bb', 21), ('csa', 'C')]\nassert sort_tuple([(\"Sarala\", 28), (\"Ayesha\", 30), (\"Suman\", 29),(\"Sai\", 21), (\"G\", \"H\")]) == [('Ayesha', 30), ('G', 'H'), ('Sai', 21), ('Sarala', 28), ('Suman', 29)]", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
