{"task_id": "Mbpp/899", "original_task_id": 899, "entry_point": "check", "prompt": "Write a python function to check whether an array can be sorted or not by picking only the corner elements.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef check(arr, n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to check whether an array can be sorted or not by picking only the corner elements.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def check(arr,n): \r\n    g = 0 \r\n    for i in range(1,n): \r\n        if (arr[i] - arr[i - 1] > 0 and g == 1): \r\n            return False\r\n        if (arr[i] - arr[i] < 0): \r\n            g = 1\r\n    return True", "tests": "assert check([3,2,1,2,3,4],6) == True\nassert check([2,1,4,5,1],5) == True\nassert check([1,2,2,1,2,3],6) == True", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/788", "original_task_id": 788, "entry_point": "new_tuple", "prompt": "Write a function to create a new tuple from the given string and list.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef new_tuple(test_list, test_str):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to create a new tuple from the given string and list.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def new_tuple(test_list, test_str):\r\n  res = tuple(test_list + [test_str])\r\n  return (res) ", "tests": "assert new_tuple([\"WEB\", \"is\"], \"best\") == ('WEB', 'is', 'best')\nassert new_tuple([\"We\", \"are\"], \"Developers\") == ('We', 'are', 'Developers')\nassert new_tuple([\"Part\", \"is\"], \"Wrong\") == ('Part', 'is', 'Wrong')", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/920", "original_task_id": 920, "entry_point": "remove_tuple", "prompt": "Write a function to remove all tuples with all none values in the given tuple list.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef remove_tuple(test_list):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to remove all tuples with all none values in the given tuple list.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def remove_tuple(test_list):\r\n  res = [sub for sub in test_list if not all(ele == None for ele in sub)]\r\n  return (str(res)) ", "tests": "assert remove_tuple([(None, 2), (None, None), (3, 4), (12, 3), (None, )] ) == '[(None, 2), (3, 4), (12, 3)]'\nassert remove_tuple([(None, None), (None, None), (3, 6), (17, 3), (None,1 )] ) == '[(3, 6), (17, 3), (None, 1)]'\nassert remove_tuple([(1, 2), (2, None), (3, None), (24, 3), (None, None )] ) == '[(1, 2), (2, None), (3, None), (24, 3)]'", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
