{"task_id": "Mbpp/838", "original_task_id": 838, "entry_point": "min_Swaps", "prompt": "Write a python function to find minimum number swaps required to make two binary strings equal.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef min_Swaps(s1, s2):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to find minimum number swaps required to make two binary strings equal.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def min_Swaps(s1,s2) :  \r\n    c0 = 0; c1 = 0;  \r\n    for i in range(len(s1)) :  \r\n        if (s1[i] == '0' and s2[i] == '1') : \r\n            c0 += 1;    \r\n        elif (s1[i] == '1' and s2[i] == '0') : \r\n            c1 += 1;  \r\n    result = c0 // 2 + c1 // 2;  \r\n    if (c0 % 2 == 0 and c1 % 2 == 0) : \r\n        return result;  \r\n    elif ((c0 + c1) % 2 == 0) : \r\n        return result + 2;  \r\n    else : \r\n        return -1;  ", "tests": "assert min_Swaps(\"0011\",\"1111\") == 1\nassert min_Swaps(\"00011\",\"01001\") == 2\nassert min_Swaps(\"111\",\"111\") == 0", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
