{"task_id": "Mbpp/713", "original_task_id": 713, "entry_point": "check_valid", "prompt": "Write a function to check if the given tuple contains all valid values or not.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef check_valid(test_tup):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to check if the given tuple contains all valid values or not.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def check_valid(test_tup):\r\n  res = not any(map(lambda ele: not ele, test_tup))\r\n  return (res) ", "tests": "assert check_valid((True, True, True, True) ) == True\nassert check_valid((True, False, True, True) ) == False\nassert check_valid((True, True, True, True) ) == True", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/681", "original_task_id": 681, "entry_point": "smallest_Divisor", "prompt": "Write a python function to find the smallest prime divisor of a number.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef smallest_Divisor(n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a python function to find the smallest prime divisor of a number.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def smallest_Divisor(n): \r\n    if (n % 2 == 0): \r\n        return 2; \r\n    i = 3;  \r\n    while (i*i <= n): \r\n        if (n % i == 0): \r\n            return i; \r\n        i += 2; \r\n    return n; ", "tests": "assert smallest_Divisor(10) == 2\nassert smallest_Divisor(25) == 5\nassert smallest_Divisor(31) == 31", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "train", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
